# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` does NOT upload to Cloud Build.
#
# `.gitignore` stays the single authority on what must never leave this machine: the include
# below pulls its entries in verbatim, so `.env` is excluded here because it is excluded
# there, and the two can't drift. Do not copy patterns out of it into this file.
#
# This file is not optional-by-omission — with a `.git` directory present, gcloud writes its
# own on the first deploy (`.gcloudignore`, `.git`, `.gitignore`, `#!include:.gitignore`).
# This is that file, reviewed, plus the build-only exclusions below.

.gcloudignore
.git
.gitignore
#!include:.gitignore

# Not needed at runtime: the Dockerfile copies pyproject.toml, src/, app.py and FE/ and
# nothing else. Adding a COPY for anything below means deleting its line here too.
tests/
scripts/
snapshots/
*.md
LICENSE
